---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Terms — Kineti" description="Software as-is under Apache-2.0. Paid setup is a separate statement of work.">
  <section class="border-b border-line">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 pt-16 pb-8 sm:px-6 sm:pt-24">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-fg sm:text-4xl">Terms</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">Minimal. Last updated 2026-08-27.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="border-b border-line">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6">
      <div class="max-w-3xl space-y-6 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">
        <p><strong class="text-fg">Software:</strong> Kineti CLI, Action, and docs are provided as-is under <a href="https://github.com/therawlogs/kineti/blob/main/LICENSE" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-accent hover:underline">Apache-2.0</a>. No warranty. No AI Act certificate.</p>
        <p><strong class="text-fg">Paid setup:</strong> Team setup (cap + required check wiring on your repos, weekly receipt export) is a separate statement of work at a fixed project fee (quote). It is not a seat license and does not include SSO, SOC 2, multi-tenant console, 24/7 SLA, or on-prem SSO — see <a href="/pricing" class="text-accent hover:underline">Pricing</a>.</p>
        <p><strong class="text-fg">Hosted:</strong> Gateway + dashboard is not generally available (waitlist). When offered, it will have its own terms.</p>
        <p><strong class="text-fg">Use:</strong> You are responsible for what model providers you route prompts to and for the code the agent writes. Verify with <code class="text-accent">ship-check</code> and <code class="text-accent">verify --all</code> before merging.</p>
        <p>Contact: waitlist on <a href="/pricing" class="text-accent hover:underline">Pricing</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
